018,1,["Origen"],["Origen: Against Celsus"],"Moreover, if the law of Moses had contained nothing which was to be understood as having a secret meaning, the prophet would not have said in his prayer to God, \"Open Thou mine eyes, and I will behold wondrous things out of Thy law;\"  whereas he knew that there was a veil of igno"],[26032005,1,["Origen"],["Origen: Against Celsus"],"Moreover, if the law of Moses had contained nothing which was to be understood as having a secret meaning, the prophet would not have said in his prayer to God, \"Open Thou mine eyes, and I will behold wondrous things out of Thy law;\"  whereas he knew that there was a veil of igno"],[28014009,1,["Origen"],["Origen: Against Celsus"]]],"f":[["Origen",2,["Against Celsus"],"Moreover, if the law of Moses had contained nothing which was to be understood as having a secret meaning, the prophet would not have said in his prayer to God, \"Open Thou mine eyes, and I will behold wondrous things out of Thy law;\"  whereas he knew that there was a veil of igno"],["Cassian",1,["The Institutes of the Coenobia"],"And so God, the Creator and Healer of all, knowing that pride is the cause and fountain head of evils, has been careful to heal opposites with opposites, that those things which were ruined by pride might be restored by humility. For the one says, \"I will ascend into heaven;\"  th"],["Chrysostom",1,["Homilies on Galatians to Philemon"],"As long as we are in the hand of God, \"no one is able to pluck us out\" (John x. 28.), for that hand is strong; but when we fall away from that hand and that help, then are we lost, then are we exposed, ready to be snatched away, as a \"bowing wall, and a tottering fence\" (Ps. lxii"]]},"4":{"l":[[40017027,7.5,"c",["G44","G2486"]],[66022002,7.4,"c",["G3319","G4215"]],[44009018,6.7,"c",["G3013"]],[40005039,5.2,"c",["G4600"]],[42006029,5.2,"c",["G4600"]],[43006009,4.9,"c",["G3795"]],[43006011,4.9,"c",["G3795"]],[43021009,4.9,"c",["G3795"]],[26038004,15.7,"s",["H2397